  "id": "ot",
  "term": "ot-",
  "definition": "OT is an abbreviation for oxytocin, a neurotransmission system discussed in psychotherapy research as being linked with parts of the therapeutic alliance such as attachment, empathy, trust, cooperation, social synchrony, and support. In this context, it is described as a possible mechanism that may help strengthen these relationship factors and relate to symptoms of depression, stress, and fear.",
